WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
Unit 1.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:04.461
Network and Transport, chapter
five, holds the design:

3
00:00:04.461 --> 00:00:09.595
Quick Access as the bridge from the V P
N, application discovery to find what's

4
00:00:09.595 --> 00:00:12.611
actually used, and then
per-app applications,

5
00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:15.300
each with its own assignment and policy.

6
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.563
Learn's Graph tutorial is the build.

7
00:00:17.563 --> 00:00:20.056
Create the app from the custom application

8
00:00:20.056 --> 00:00:22.412
template and mark it a Private Access app.

9
00:00:22.412 --> 00:00:24.288
Bind it to one connector group.

10
00:00:24.288 --> 00:00:29.025
Add only the segments it uses:
one host, its ports, its protocol.

11
00:00:29.025 --> 00:00:31.449
Assign a group, with the app's User role;

12
00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:34.812
not individuals, and nested
groups aren't supported.

13
00:00:34.812 --> 00:00:40.052
Then put Conditional Access on it, in
report-only first, following Learn's example:

14
00:00:40.052 --> 00:00:44.587
multifactor authentication and a
compliant or hybrid-joined device,

15
00:00:44.587 --> 00:00:46.699
with emergency access excluded.

16
00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:49.975
Learn's rules: segments may
not overlap between apps,

17
00:00:49.975 --> 00:00:54.850
except that a per-app segment overrides
an overlapping Quick Access segment.

18
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:57.937
Clients take up to fifteen
minutes to pick up a change.

19
00:00:57.937 --> 00:01:03.470
And Microsoft advises against an M F
A sign-in frequency on Quick Access,

20
00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:06.430
because D N S queries trigger prompts.
